# ── Target Go Application ───────────────────────────
PORT=8080
DATA_DIR=./data

# Base URL for absolute media/API URLs. The dev default pairs with the Vite
# proxy — change both together. Production must be https.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# development | production — production enables Secure session cookies.
APP_ENV=development

# Canonical browser origin for origin/CSRF checks. Production has NO default
# and fails closed unless an explicit https origin is set.
TRUSTED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────
# SMTP_API_KEY (Resend API key) is NOT a process env var for
# the app. Under docker compose it reaches the app as a Compose file secret
# mounted at /run/secrets/smtp_api_key (compose.yaml `secrets:` block, value
# read from the VPS .env). The local dev server (`go run`, `make dev-local`)
# ignores it and runs without the secret; production fails closed without
# it once a feature consumes it. Never commit a real value here.

# ── SMTP relay ───────────────────────────────────────
# Empty SMTP_HOST = the dev LogLink mailer: reset links are LOGGED instead
# of sent. That is loopback-only — config validation refuses it unless
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL is http://localhost:3000. Set SMTP_HOST to use a real
# relay (production requires it). Resend: host smtp.resend.com, port 587
# (STARTTLS) or 465 (implicit TLS); username is the literal "resend".
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USERNAME=resend
# Development default sender: the verified root domain.
# The old onboarding@resend.dev default can only reach the Resend account
# owner's own inbox (403 for everyone else). Production requires an
# explicit SMTP_FROM (fail-closed).
SMTP_FROM=noreply@sickfansubs.com
# No Reply-To header exists: the From is a no-reply
# sender and replies are meant to bounce.

# ── Web push ─────────────────────────────────────────
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY is NOT a process env var for the app: under docker
# compose it reaches the app as a Compose file secret mounted at
# /run/secrets/vapid_private_key (compose.yaml `secrets:` block, value read
# from the VPS .env). The local dev server runs without it — web push
# delivery is DISABLED (the subscription/preference endpoints still work);
# production refuses to start without it (fail-closed) and also checks that
# the private half matches VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY (config.ValidateVAPIDPair).
# The committed VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY below is the PRODUCTION pair's public half
# (installed 2026-09-21): the matching private half exists ONLY in the VPS
# .env, so a locally generated pair will NOT match it. Rotation:
# bunx web-push generate-vapid-keys, put the private half in the VPS .env,
# swap the four committed copies together (web constant, Go default, this
# file, the compose fallback) — the pin tests fail until they agree.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BHTZD8cRI0vmAwkO9fcsY7KwL2vL7vx1OByBARaSItTq2kqQNiPqLJa7zHSIgj8yRlAxGgO5ZAvxwMyMeNqafdc
